			<item>				<title>Scheduled Upgrade</title>
				<description>Between Friday the 2nd at Midnight and Saturday the 4th at 4AM, web services will become temporarily 
unavailable.  We will be upgrading hardware, and it shouldn&apos;t keep the site down for more than 
30 minutes.</description>
				<link>http://www.guildportal.com</link>
				<author>Aaron Lewis</author>
				<pubDate>Thu, 01 Jul 2004 01:51:00 GMT</pubDate>
			</item>
			<item>				<title>Themes and Styles</title>
				<description>Hey all!  Thanks to the folks who have been submitting their themes -- we&apos;ve got quite a few now that you can import from your Control Panel!  For those who are currently using Custom CSS (in Advanced Styles), we&apos;ve also made many new classes available for you to totally customize the appearance of your forums.  This is the first part of a series of things we&apos;re going to be providing to make the site style customization even more powerful.  There are tools coming to simplify managing styles, that do not require the use of Custom CSS, but for the time being we&apos;ve released the new style classes for those who want to get a jump on customizing their forum appearance.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A full listing of the classes that can be added to your Custom CSS can be found &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.guildportal.com/Guild.aspx?GuildID=3780&amp;ForumID=22042&amp;TabID=27537&amp;TopicID=541760&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.</description>
				<link>http://www.guildportal.com</link>
				<author>Aaron Lewis</author>
				<pubDate>Mon, 28 Jun 2004 08:27:00 GMT</pubDate>
			</item>
			<item>				<title>Event Attendance</title>
				<description>Heya!  Before this morning&apos;s push, members needed to sign up for events before they could be awarded Raid Points and have reporting on attendance show their in-game event attendance appropriately.  Now, once an event follow-up is saved, event admins are given the opportunity to mark people as attended that did not originally sign up.  Additionally, you have the option to modify the Raid Point value of a given event specifically for people who did not sign up, in case any kind of penalty is appropriate for your specific scenario.</description>
				<link>http://www.guildportal.com</link>
				<author>Aaron Lewis</author>
				<pubDate>Mon, 21 Jun 2004 08:15:00 GMT</pubDate>
			</item>
			<item>				<title>Theme Submissions</title>
				<description>Hey folks!  If you&apos;ve got a great-looking site with appealing colors, custom HTML, custom CSS or other elements that you think other admins might like to import (credit to the author given, of course), you can now submit your site&apos;s style settings as a Theme!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In the Control Panel, click on &quot;Styles &amp;amp; Colors,&quot; then click on &quot;Submit Theme!&quot;</description>
				<link>http://www.guildportal.com</link>
				<author>Aaron Lewis</author>
				<pubDate>Fri, 11 Jun 2004 13:28:00 GMT</pubDate>
			</item>
			<item>				<title>Custom Welcome Messages</title>
				<description>You can now configure custom welcome messages for all of the different security levels.  Existing welcome messages are the &quot;default,&quot; and you can add custom ones either by going to your control panel and modifying the content, or by clicking on the pencil icon underneath a welcome message content type you already have on your pages.</description>
				<link>http://www.guildportal.com</link>
				<author>Aaron Lewis</author>
				<pubDate>Thu, 10 Jun 2004 13:36:00 GMT</pubDate>
			</item>
			<item>				<title>Idle Monitor Enhancement</title>
				<description>The Idle Monitor now has a link called &quot;Manage Exemptions,&quot; which allows the selection of members of the guild to be exempt from Idle Monitor processing.  Members marked as Exempt will not receive warnings and will not be auto-disbanded (if these options are enabled in the Idle Monitor to begin with).  This ensures that people who have given away-time notice that is approved by guild leaders are not hassled by the site.  &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Note that members with Officer or higher level access, and members that have not yet been approved as members, will never be processed by the Idle Monitor, so it is not necessary to add them to the exemption list.  &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A section has been added to the &lt;a href=&quot;/FAQ.aspx?FAQEntry=52&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Frequently Asked Questions&lt;/a&gt; that gives an overview on the Idle Monitor and the Exemptions.</description>
				<link>http://www.guildportal.com</link>
				<author>Aaron Lewis</author>
				<pubDate>Thu, 10 Jun 2004 09:20:00 GMT</pubDate>
			</item>
			<item>				<title>Idle Monitor Live</title>
				<description>We&apos;ve added new functionality to the Control Panel called the &quot;Idle Monitor.&quot;  You get to it by clicking on &quot;Site Members&quot; and then &quot;Idle Monitor&quot; from the Task list.  Many thanks to the individual who recommended this at the most recent Fan Faire GuildPortal attended!&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Using this tool, SuperAdmins can have the system automatically send out customized warning e-mails to members who have been inactive for a configurable number of days.  Additionally, you can also tell the system to automatically disband anybody who has not been on for a configurable number of days, also sending an e-mail (perhaps with instructions on re-joining).&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;The process that manages warning e-mails and auto-disbanding runs every other night, and will send a summary message to all appropriate admins, listing all actions that it took during a given run.</description>
				<link>http://www.guildportal.com</link>
				<author>Aaron Lewis</author>
				<pubDate>Tue, 08 Jun 2004 05:20:00 GMT</pubDate>
			</item>
			<item>				<title>Some Updates</title>
				<description>Hello all!  We&apos;ve updated the &lt;a href=&quot;FAQ.aspx&quot;&gt;Frequently Asked Questions&lt;/a&gt; page with some more information on character management, subscriptions, administration, and some general information on GuildPortal.  Also, there was a bug where guild bans on individuals by user name wouldn&apos;t always take hold (currently bans work on both user name and IP address -- though the IP is hidden to protect privacy), and code has been pushed to fix it.</description>
				<link>http://www.guildportal.com</link>
				<author>Aaron Lewis</author>
				<pubDate>Mon, 07 Jun 2004 01:18:00 GMT</pubDate>
			</item>
			<item>				<title>New Calendar</title>
				<description>Hey all!  There&apos;s a new content type available, called &quot;Calendar (Enhanced).&quot;  Aside from a cleaner interface, this new calendar shows not only sign-ups from the guild that created an event, but also (in the case of alliance events) sign-ups from all allied guilds, as well.  Also, members can now sign up for events with more than one character, for those multi-taskers in the guild.  More enhancements surrounding the new calendar are coming!</description>
				<link>http://www.guildportal.com</link>
				<author>Aaron Lewis</author>
				<pubDate>Tue, 25 May 2004 12:03:00 GMT</pubDate>
			</item>
			<item>				<title>Game News Content Type</title>
				<description>Great news, admins!  You no longer need to specify which game news feed you want displayed on your pages -- the standard &quot;Game News&quot; content type will now retrieve game news for your guild&apos;s game from the appropriate source.  Further, aside from game developer-provided news feeds, external news for 10 of the games GuildPortal supports is now coming directly from the &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.warcry.com&quot;&gt;Warcry&lt;/a&gt; network!  Clicking on a news item from one of the Warcry-supported games takes you to the news item on the Warcry site itself.  While you&apos;re there, check out all of the great content they have available!&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; Many thanks to Rhomany for getting the information we needed to implement these feeds!</description>
				<link>http://www.guildportal.com</link>
				<author>Aaron Lewis</author>
				<pubDate>Thu, 20 May 2004 10:23:00 GMT</pubDate>
			</item>
